WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.432
Model selection starts in week 1, too.

2
00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:06.275
Scoping is also where you set up the evidence for model choices.

3
00:00:06.555 --> 00:00:23.963
Your eval set and baseline let you answer questions that otherwise turn into opinion: does the frontier model beat a cheaper tier on this task, does an open-weight model running locally meet the bar for a privacy-sensitive user, does a long-context call do as well as retrieval?

4
00:00:24.243 --> 00:00:39.155
Write down the candidates you expect to compare (for example, two tiers from one provider and one model from another provider or an open model), and the guard metrics that would decide between them, such as cost per task and p95 latency.

5
00:00:39.435 --> 00:00:41.099
Don’t run that comparison yet.

6
00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:51.192
The point in week 1 is that you will be able to run it later, on the same cases, with paired statistics, instead of picking a model because it is the one you used last.

7
00:00:51.472 --> 00:00:57.488
That is the habit a working team needs most: a standing eval set that turns “should we switch models?

8
00:00:57.768 --> 00:01:00.072
” from a meeting into a one-command run.
